course: dictionary
lesson: 12253
title: Construct: build, draw and make
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Construct» means to build or make something carefully, putting parts together to make a whole. You can use it for a house, a bridge or a model made from card.
explain: In maths, «construct» is an instruction. «Construct a triangle with sides 5 cm, 6 cm and 7 cm» means draw it exactly, using a ruler, compasses and protractor, not by guessing with your eye.
explain: You can also use «construct» for words and ideas. «Construct a sentence» means put words together in the right order, and «construct an argument» means build a clear reason for what you think. The words around it show you which meaning fits.
fact: Construct is a verb: I construct, he constructs, we constructed, they are constructing.
fact: «Construct» means to build or make something, such as a house, bridge or model.
fact: In maths, «construct» means to draw a shape accurately with a ruler, compasses and protractor.
fact: «Construct» can also be a noun, meaning an idea made by people's minds rather than found in nature.
fact: «Well constructed» means built strongly and carefully.
exercise: «The class will construct a model bridge from paper and card.» What does construct mean here? | To look at carefully | To break apart | *To build or make | To sing about
exercise: «Use your ruler and compasses to construct a triangle.» What does construct mean in maths? | Colour the shape in | *Draw the shape accurately with tools | Cut the shape out of paper | Guess the shape by eye
exercise: Which phrase means putting words together in the right order? | construct a model car | *construct a sentence | construct a bridge
exercise: «The engineers construct the bridge over the river.» What does construct mean? | To clean | To paint | *To build | To forget
exercise: In «The theory is a clever construct of the mind», what is a construct? | A loud noise | A tall tree | A river bank | *An idea made by people's minds
exam: Which is the maths meaning of «construct»? | *Draw it accurately with a ruler, compasses and protractor | Guess the shape by eye | Rub it out | Colour it in
